				"string" : "modern system such as clojure on the jvm lacks tail call optimisation so functions seem a bit twisted , perhaps f sharp language may come to help .\nSmalltalk has many side effects , spend a  large amount of time in browser , seems unstable especially pharo , the file in - file out debacle where code in system looks different when serialized - many incompatible versions. something like common lisp has been around for many many years and is pretty fast but is also hindered by side effects . \nstandard ml functional programming but libraries are lacking , \njavascript has a large libraryt collection and a total lack of security , especially wide ranging damage a bad import can have on an editor used for cryptography keys stolen by javascript script.\nmodel view controller intimately tied together. \nweb api is agnostic no memory between transactions.\nwhat qualities do want in software system ?\n1 - should be reliable\n2 - should be easy to debug\n3 - should cope with change - different computer - do i have to rewrite everything from scratch , \nadvantage of java jvm , write once run everywhere\n4 - multi processor computing  , smalltalk user interface freeszes up when a request is made , nothing to indicate what it is doing at all\n5 - moldable development - glamorous toolkit - tools visualise changes , perhaps better spent dumping into html and allowing javascript to handle with css flurry front end madness\n6 - need to be comfortable in the language using , should be good documentation , up to date with plenty of examples on how to use it\n7 - over dependence on user interface clouds real thinking required to solve real problems \n8 - prefer a simple text user interface over complex\n9 - what if the computation takes hours or weeks , what is to be displayed on the machine , \n10 - imp"
			}
		]
